# Solidity / Foundry Rules

## Style
- Use Solidity 0.8.x with the latest stable compiler
- Follow the Solidity style guide: contract-level NatSpec on all public/external functions
- Use `forge fmt` formatting (do not fight it)
- Errors must be custom errors (not `require` strings) for gas efficiency
- Events for all state mutations
- Use OpenZeppelin contracts from `lib/` (git submodules)

## Security Checklist
Before any PR, verify:
- Reentrancy guards on external calls that transfer value
- Access control on admin functions (Ownable or role-based)
- Slippage protection on all swap/liquidity operations
- No floating pragma — pin exact compiler version
- Check-effects-interactions pattern
- Integer overflow is handled (Solidity 0.8+ default, but verify for unchecked blocks)

## Testing
- Write tests in Solidity (not JavaScript) using `forge test`
- Use `forge test --fork-url` for integration tests against live state
- Fuzz tests for math-heavy functions (bonding curve calculations)
- Invariant tests for protocol-level properties
- Name test files `*.t.sol`, place in `test/`
- Name test functions `test_<description>` for passing, `testFail_<description>` for expected reverts, `testFuzz_<description>` for fuzz tests

## Deployment
- Use `forge script` (not `forge create`) for reproducible deployments
- Scripts go in `script/`, named `Deploy<Contract>.s.sol`
- Never hardcode private keys — use `cast wallet import` encrypted keystores
